    "description": "Nikkato Corporation manufactures and sells industrial ceramic consumables in Japan. The company operates through the Ceramics Business and Engineering Business segments. The Ceramics Business segment manufactures and sells ceramic tools; fixtures; tubes; protection and insulating tubes; firing containers; crucibles; setters; balls; wear-resistant components; and machine parts used in the production processes of manufacturers of electronic components, food, pharmaceuticals, paints, and other products, as well as ceramics and other materials for scientific and chemical use. The Engineering Business segment purchases and sells measurement and control equipment, heating equipment, and temperature sensors. It also offers electric furnaces and laboratory porcelain. The company was founded in 1913 and is headquartered in Sakai, Japan."
